{
  "_comment": "SYNTHETIC test cases for M-02 parser m02-text-parser/1. Not DrugBank content, no clinical meaning. Expected results written from RULES.md before implementation.",
  "author": "author-tmax-refs",
  "ambiguities": [
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] Peak plasma concentrations are reached within 0.5-1 hours after oral administration.", "why": "RULES 4 makes 'within' an inclusive upper_bound in Tmax context but does not say what kind results when 'within' precedes a range (range 0.5..1 vs upper_bound 1); the no-'within' variant is used as a case instead."},
    {"text": "(empty / whitespace-only absorption, and 'Not Available')", "why": "Every case text must start with '[SYNTHETIC] ', which makes it non-empty and not an exact placeholder string, so empty/placeholder statuses (RULES 2.1-2.2) cannot be expressed under that constraint."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] Peak plasma concentrations are reached over 2 hours.", "why": "RULES 4 says 'over' -> review (ambiguous_qualifier) but not whether this yields a review-flagged measurement (parsed_needs_review) or only a review item (unparsed_needs_review)."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] Peak plasma concentrations of the depot are reached 1 month after injection.", "why": "unit_not_exactly_convertible: RULES does not say whether a flagged measurement with null hours is kept or only a review item is written."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] In children aged 2-12 years, peak plasma concentration was reached 1 hour after oral administration.", "why": "Unclear whether a context-excluded duration ('aged 2-12 years') still counts as a duration for window splitting (RULES 3), so whether 'children' stays on the Tmax value is undetermined."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] Absorption was studied in children aged 2-12 years.", "why": "An excluded age duration goes to review per RULES 5, which would make the field unparsed_needs_review rather than no_statement_found; not certain this is intended for age expressions with no Tmax keyword."},
    {"text": "[SYNTHETIC] Tmax is 1 hour after oral administration of the solution, whereas the suspension reaches peak plasma concentrations at 3 hours.", "why": "RULES 6 says time_reference comes from 'window/sentence'; unclear whether 'after ... administration' in window 1 gives window 2 after_administration (conditions must not carry over, but the time reference rule mentions the sentence)."}
  ],
